\* All TLC check configs for AntflyHATimelineSwitch.tla, one section per check.
\* Sections are verbatim TLC config syntax; the build extracts them
\* (scripts/tla-cfg.sh). Section names match the make-target check ids.

==== positive tier=fast
\* TLC config for AntflyHATimelineSwitch.tla

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggySwitchBeforeApplied = FALSE
    BuggyNonMonotonicSwitch = FALSE
    BuggyAcceptOldTimeline = FALSE
    BuggyRecoverWrongPrevious = FALSE

INVARIANTS
    TypeOK
    ProgressOrder
    SwitchRecordIsMonotonic
    SwitchRequiresAppliedProgress
    SwitchRecordIsContiguous
    SwitchedIdentityMatchesRecord
    OldTimelineRejectedAfterSwitch
    RecoveryUsesRecoveredProgress
    Safety

==== BadBeforeApplied
\* Expected-failure config: a timeline switch is accepted before parent
\* received/applied/safe progress has caught up.
\* Pinned to the specific semantic invariant this mutant must violate.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggySwitchBeforeApplied = TRUE
    BuggyNonMonotonicSwitch = FALSE
    BuggyAcceptOldTimeline = FALSE
    BuggyRecoverWrongPrevious = FALSE

INVARIANTS
    SwitchRequiresAppliedProgress

==== BadNonMonotonic
\* Expected-failure config: a timeline switch record can reuse the current
\* timeline or epoch.
\* Pinned to the specific semantic invariant this mutant must violate.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggySwitchBeforeApplied = FALSE
    BuggyNonMonotonicSwitch = TRUE
    BuggyAcceptOldTimeline = FALSE
    BuggyRecoverWrongPrevious = FALSE

INVARIANTS
    SwitchRecordIsMonotonic

==== BadOldTimeline
\* Expected-failure config: after switching, an old-timeline record is accepted.
\* Pinned to the specific semantic invariant this mutant must violate.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggySwitchBeforeApplied = FALSE
    BuggyNonMonotonicSwitch = FALSE
    BuggyAcceptOldTimeline = TRUE
    BuggyRecoverWrongPrevious = FALSE

INVARIANTS
    OldTimelineRejectedAfterSwitch

==== BadRecoveryPrevious
\* Expected-failure config: crash recovery applies a durable timeline switch
\* whose previous_lsn is not contiguous with recovered parent progress.
\* Pinned to the specific semantic invariant this mutant must violate.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggySwitchBeforeApplied = FALSE
    BuggyNonMonotonicSwitch = FALSE
    BuggyAcceptOldTimeline = FALSE
    BuggyRecoverWrongPrevious = TRUE

INVARIANTS
    RecoveryUsesRecoveredProgress
